    "readout_text": "To find \\( f(2023) \\), we start by recognizing that the function \\( f \\) satisfies the condition:\n\n\\[\n\\sum_{d \\mid n} d \\cdot f\\left(\\frac{n}{d}\\right) = 1\n\\]\n\nThis can be interpreted as the Dirichlet convolution of the identity function \\( \\text{id} \\) and \\( f \\) resulting in the constant function \\( \\mathbf{1} \\). Thus, \\( f \\) is the Dirichlet inverse of \\( \\text{id} \\).\n\nTo compute \\( f(n) \\), we use the formula:\n\n\\[\nf(n) = \\sum_{d \\mid n} \\mu(d) \\cdot d\n\\]\n\nwhere \\( \\mu \\) is the Möbius function. Factoring \\( 2023 \\) as \\( 7 \\times 17^2 \\), its divisors are \\( 1, 7, 17, 17^2, 7 \\times 17, 7 \\times 17^2 \\). Calculating \\( \\mu(d) \\) for each divisor and summing \\( \\mu(d) \\cdot d \\) yields:\n\n\\[\nf(2023) = 1 - 7 - 17 + 119 = 96\n\\]\n\n**Answer:** \\(\\boxed{96}\\)",
